      "writtenOn": "2024-11-13T12:27:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I took a closer look since Vincent\u0027s spinlock answer didn\u0027t convince me at all! I believe that trace_clock_update *is* already serialised at its caller, which unhelpfully is in a later patch in this series (aosp/3343946):\n1. That later patch hooks trace_clock_update() into a hypercall named __pkvm_update_clock_tracing. This is the sole caller of this function.\n2. The hypercall is called only from a periodic work item, __hyp_clock_work(). This periodically runs itself via workqueue, and thus is implicitly non-reentrant.",
